---
title: Binary space partition rooms
---
Rooms placed in ever-smaller parts of the map, so they come out better spaced than random rooms [[t:61-64 s:7]].

## The rule
1. Start a list with one rectangle inside the map’s edge, and that rectangle’s four quarters [[c02:24-29 c02:87-111]].
2. **Repeat 240 times** [[c02:41-54]]:
   1. pick any rectangle on the list [[c02:43 c02:114-120]];
   2. try a room near its top-left corner [[c02:44 c02:122-136]];
   3. if every tile within 2 of the room is solid and inside the map’s outer ring, carve the room [[c02:45-49 c02:138-174]];
   4. then add the four quarters of the rectangle it came from to the list [[c02:50 c02:86-112]].
3. Sort the rooms by their left edge, and join each to the one before it with a corridor [[c02:57-78]].

@@diagram bsp-quarters alt="A rectangle cut into four quarters, each tinted differently. A small room sits near the top-left corner of the first quarter, and another near the top-left corner of the last." caption="The demo’s list holds a rectangle’s four quarters (tinted). A room is tried near the top-left corner of whichever rectangle is picked."
aaaaaaabbbbbbb
a...aaabbbbbbb
a...aaabbbbbbb
aaaaaaabbbbbbb
cccccccddddddd
cccccccd...ddd
cccccccd...ddd
cccccccddddddd

- **Talk says:** halve the map, then each half, until a piece is about the size of a room [[t:66-69]].
- **Demo:** looser. It cuts into quarters, keeps every rectangle it has cut on its list, and quarters a rectangle again each time a room lands in it [[c02:41-55 c02:86-121]].

## Step-through
@@steps limit=6

## Controls
@@control attempts
Times a rectangle is picked and a room tried. The demo’s counter goes up on every attempt, whether or not the room fits [[c02:41-55]].

## Measured traits
@@measured

- **Talk says:** its animation shows absolutely no rejections [[t:70-72]].
- **BSP rooms:** of 240 attempts, {{c02.rooms.median}} place a room at the median [[run:c02.rooms.median]].
  - **Why none are seen:** the demo records a frame only for a room that fits [[c02:41-55]].
- **vs random rooms:** {{c02.rooms.median}} rooms vs {{c01.rooms.median}}; floor share {{c02.floor_share.median}} vs {{c01.floor_share.median}} [[run:c02.rooms.median c01.rooms.median c02.floor_share.median c01.floor_share.median]].

